{"t":"2026-05-20T20:16:28.874Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01KX4MGe6rMqSST6ZsR59MDm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I understand. The tool handler is trying to construct schemas with fields that don't match. The correct approach is:\n\n1. `DiscoveredJobSchema` requires `source`, `source_id`, `title`, `company`, `url` (not `candidate_id`, `url_hash`)\n2. `ScoredJobSchema` requires `discovered_job_id`, `candidate_id`, `score_breakdown`, `composite_score`, `reasoning` (not `job`, `scores`)\n\nThe `JDParser.parse` method expects a `ScoredJobSchema` that has `.job` as a nested `DiscoveredJobSchema`. This appears to be a structural mismatch from the original design.\n\nLet me check if there's a historical version or if the schemas have been migrated:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":719,"cache_read_input_tokens":73944,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":719,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78b056f7-705e-4dcd-b620-10cb1067f6bf","uuid":"a4c497fe-8a2a-4a85-8a73-dcc5b98d69a2"}}
