{"t":"2026-05-20T20:17:04.718Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01QwQpwUNvbcV7VA6x9hYhT7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"So the ORM model `DiscoveredJob` does NOT have `candidate_id` or `url_hash` fields. These fields are in a different model (likely `ScoredJob` has `candidate_id`). Looking at the orchestrator code using `job_orm.candidate_id` and `job_orm.url_hash` is incorrect.\n\nBut wait—this is in the **orchestrator**, not in the **agent_manager**. The agent_manager is in MY scope, and the orchestrator is part of the apply-agent scope.\n\nLet me review the HYPHA again to ensure I understand my scope:\n\nAccording to HYPHA-AGENT-MANAGER.md:\n- **My scope**: AgentManager, SubAgentRegistry, SubAgentRunner, PipelineDispatcher, AgentExecutionRecord\n- **Out of scope**: The per-agent business logic (lives in `application-engine` modules; this biome calls them as tool handlers)\n\nSo the issue with the orchestrator code referencing non-existent fields is out of my scope. However, the **tool handlers in agent_manager.py** that try to call the per-agent code are in my scope, and they need to work correctly.\n\nLet me look at the issue more carefully. The tool handlers need to bridge Claude's tool_use calls to the real agent code. The tool handler `handle_parse_jd` is trying to create schemas that don't match reality.\n\nLooking at HYPHA-AGENT-MANAGER.md notes:\n> Tool handlers in `_register_tool_handlers` reconstruct Pydantic schemas from the input dict (e.g., `ParsedJDSchema(**input_data[\"parsed_jd\"])`). Schema drift will break tool handlers — schema-core is the gate.\n\nThis tells me the tool handlers should reconstruct schemas from the input, but the current implementation is creating invalid schemas. The fix should be to align the tool handlers with the actual schema definitions.\n\nLet me now fix the tool handler to work with the actual schemas. The key issue is that `JDParser.parse()` expects a `ScoredJobSchema` with a `.job` attribute that has `.id`, `.title`, `.company`, `.description`, `.location`. But `ScoredJobSchema` doesn't have a `.job` attribute - it has denormalized fields.\n\nThis is a fundamental mismatch in the existing code. The JDParser is expecting an old schema structure. Since I can't modify the JDParser (it's out of my scope as apply-agent owns it), I need to create a compatible wrapper in my tool handler.\n\nLet me create a solution:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":674,"cache_read_input_tokens":79327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":674,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78b056f7-705e-4dcd-b620-10cb1067f6bf","uuid":"23d74b0a-96e8-4478-8d58-758752f565c8"}}
