{"t":"2026-05-20T20:17:30.318Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_018tkGsxuoc41mPfeYCwtGxQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The ORM model has `discovered_job` relationship. So when loading from DB with relationship loaded, `scored_job_orm.discovered_job` will give access to the discovered job. The schema serialization should include this.\n\nThe issue is the Pydantic schema `ScoredJobSchema` doesn't include a `job` field - it only has denormalized fields. The orchestrator's `_load_scored_job` method should be creating a wrapper that includes the relationship, but the schema doesn't support it.\n\nSince this is a **schema drift** issue that exists in the apply-agent's code (orchestrator + JDParser), and my hypha states:\n> Schema drift will break tool handlers — schema-core is the gate.\n\nThis means the schema-core (data-agent) should have the correct schemas, and the apply-agent should have fixed their code. Since I can't modify those, I need to create a compatible adapter in my tool handlers.\n\nThe simplest fix is to create a wrapper class or dict structure that matches what JDParser expects. Let me look at what JDParser actually accesses:\n\nFrom `jd_parser.py`:\n- `job.job.id` (line 53)\n- `job.job.title` (line 54)\n- `job.job.company` (line 54)\n- `job.job.description` (line 95)\n- `job.job.location` (line 100)\n\nSo JDParser expects `ScoredJobSchema` to have a `.job` attribute that is a `DiscoveredJobSchema`. The Pydantic schema doesn't have this, but I can create an adapter.\n\nLet me update the tool handler to create a proper adapter:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":468,"cache_read_input_tokens":81716,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":468,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78b056f7-705e-4dcd-b620-10cb1067f6bf","uuid":"108f7f0f-d318-426c-9673-d0ef143618d5"}}
